    "sentence_translations": [
      "Do you want to eat the All In Hamburger?",
      "",
      "From April 28th to May 31st, the fast food chain Lotteria introduces an “All In Hamburger” in Japan.",
      "Put simply, it's a hamburger that has everything.",
      "",
      "This hamburger uses all the hamburger ingredients in the store.",
      "It has all kinds of meat, ribs, fried shrimp, egg, cheese, lettuce, etc.",
      "On top of that it has 6 sauces including ketchup and salad dressing, making it an over ten centimeters tall hamburger.",
      "The hamburger costs 1350 Japanese yen, or approximately 80 Chinese yuan.",
      "",
      "Lotteria originally introduced this hamburger in 2013.",
      "It is only now in 2016 that they finally reintroduce it.",
      "It is said that because the people who ate it last time have just finished digesting, ..",
      ".. so they waited until now to reintroduce the hamburger.",
      "If you are in Japan and a big eater you can try going to Lotteria to try out this hamburger."
    ]
